                <pb facs="0728" n="634" xml:id="pg634"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Armstrong to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received June 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 527.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your No. 506, of the 13th ultimo, to Minister Taylor, relative to the
                    detention of George Calvar and Peter Duarte, citizens of the United States, by
                    the Spanish military authorities in Cuba in violation of the treaty of 1795 and
                    the protocol of January 12, 1877, and to inform you that the case has been duly
                    presented to the Spanish Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Clay Armstrong</hi>, Jr.,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
